# `ix` names the index of the loop it stands in (Semantics ch. 5: "with `ix` and `jx` as in
# every loop"); outside a loop it names nothing. prismc's back end refuses it today ("`ix`
# outside a `for`"); the checker should. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch;
# subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

Next: fn Nat -> Nat
fn Next n = n + ix

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Next 1}")
